{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Ho Ariel.</b> Some say Jerusalem is so called after the altar, like וההראל and האריאל (Ezekiel 43:15–16), for the letters yod, heh, vav, alef interchange. Some say it is so called because its constellation is Arieh [Leo]; this is far-fetched." "<b>City of.</b> Construct state, and the word emet or its like is missing." "<b>[Where David encamped].</b> That David encamped there, or thus is the way of language to attach to a past verb, like the beginning of the word of YHWH (Hosea 1:2)." "<b>Add year.</b> Add a year, like לספות עוד (Numbers 32:14)." "And <b>חגים</b> are the burnt offerings." "<b>ינקופו.</b> Intransitive verb, and the meaning is that the burnt offerings will cease; or it may be a transitive verb with the word הנוקפים missing, like ויאמר ליוסף (Genesis 48:1)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {2 "Bracketed lemma head as given in source; the phrase תחלת דבר יי from Hosea is compared to Genesis 1:1 as an example of construct attached to a clause, cited mid-sentence."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:46.685068333Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}